+## Session startup failure handling
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator still rejects to the caller, invokes `onError` with `(session, error)`, and then invokes `afterSession` with `(session)` ([validated by: runs onError with session and error, then afterSession, and rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionThrow.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- Because `afterSession` fires even when `beforeSession` fails, `afterSession` must not assume `beforeSession` completed or that any per-turn state was allocated: `beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, `afterModelResponse`, and `provider.sendMessage` never run on that path ([validated by: skips user, model, and provider phases when beforeSession throws on stream](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionThrow.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
